 "code": "await rlm.harness.create_memory(title='ARC open-top rectangular frame with directional beam', content='Task-5b54e9f6: A 5-colored incomplete rectangular frame is a 4x4 outline with one missing cell in the top edge, while other three sides are complete. Fill every 0 in the rectangle interior with 2; also fill the missing top-edge cell with 2. Extend a horizontal 2 beam outward from the missing top cell, along the row immediately above the frame, toward the side where the remaining top-edge segment is longer (equivalently away from the shorter remaining segment). Beam continues to grid edge. Demonstrations: frame bbox row3-6 col2-5, top missing col4; left top segment length2 vs right1, beam extends left on row2 col0..4; interiors filled. Second bbox row3-7 col3-6, top missing col4; left top segment length1 vs right2, beam extends right on row2 col4..9. Test had frames bbox r1-4 c1-4 missing top c3 (beam left on r0 c0..3) and bbox r7-9 c5-8 missing top c8 (left top portion c6-7 longer than right c9; beam left on row6 c0..7); interiors color2. Colors: outline 5, fill 2, background 0. All examples validate the rule; tested submission correct.",
